`accepted` MEANS `the insurer has accepted provisional liability`
`taken to have accepted` MEANS `the insurer is taken to have accepted provisional liability`
`not accepted` MEANS `the insurer has not accepted provisional liability`
`still time` MEANS `the insurer still has time to give notice`

-- Form received 1 June 2015: the 10 days end on 11 June 2015.
-- Arguments: received; notice given; notice day; accepts; Nominal Defendant for an unidentified vehicle; today.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) TRUE (`d` 5 6 2015) TRUE FALSE (`d` 20 6 2015) EQUALS `accepted`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) TRUE (`d` 11 6 2015) FALSE FALSE (`d` 20 6 2015) EQUALS `not accepted`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) TRUE (`d` 12 6 2015) FALSE FALSE (`d` 20 6 2015) EQUALS `taken to have accepted`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) TRUE (`d` 12 6 2015) FALSE TRUE (`d` 20 6 2015) EQUALS `not accepted`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 11 6 2015) EQUALS `still time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE (`d` 12 6 2015) EQUALS `taken to have accepted`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) FALSE `any day` FALSE TRUE (`d` 12 6 2015) EQUALS `not accepted`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted provisional liability` (`d` 1 6 2015) TRUE (`d` 20 6 2015) TRUE TRUE (`d` 20 6 2015) EQUALS `accepted`

-- Arguments: treatment expenses; lost earnings; the maximum.
