#ASSERT `How much early payment must the insurer make` 6000 1000 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `How much early payment must the insurer make` 4000 2500 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `How much early payment must the insurer make` 0 7000 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `How much early payment must the insurer make` 5000 0 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `How much early payment must the insurer make` 2000 1000 6000 EQUALS 3000

§§ `ss 70, 72 -- reporting and claiming`

#ASSERT `By when must I report the accident to police` (`d` 1 3 2015) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 3 2015)
#ASSERT `By when must I report the accident to police` (`d` 1 3 2015) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: accident day; claim for a death; day of death.
#ASSERT `By when must I make my claim` (`d` 15 1 2015) FALSE `any day` EQUALS `d` 15 7 2015
-- 31 August plus six months: the last day of February (leap and common years).
#ASSERT `By when must I make my claim` (`d` 31 8 2015) FALSE `any day` EQUALS `d` 29 2 2016
#ASSERT `By when must I make my claim` (`d` 31 8 2014) FALSE `any day` EQUALS `d` 28 2 2015
-- A death: six months from the death, not the accident.
#ASSERT `By when must I make my claim` (`d` 1 1 2015) TRUE (`d` 10 2 2015) EQUALS `d` 10 8 2015

§§ `ss 34A, 70, 73, 76 -- the insurer's two months`

-- Claim received 15 January 2016: the two months end on 15 March 2016 (day 60).
-- Arguments: ground; received; what the insurer did; when; explanation given; when received; explanation rejected; when; today.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `nothing done` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 15 3 2016) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `nothing done` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 16 3 2016) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `rejected` (`d` 15 3 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 1 2017) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `rejected` (`d` 16 3 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 1 2017) EQUALS TRUE
-- Asked on 1 February; explanation received 1 April: the second two months end on 1 June 2016.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 1 2 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2016) FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 6 2016) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 1 2 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2016) FALSE `any day` (`d` 2 6 2016) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 1 2 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2016) (`d` 1 1 2017) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 1 2 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2016) TRUE (`d` 2 6 2016) (`d` 1 1 2017) EQUALS TRUE
-- An explanation after an early rejection still starts the second two months (s 73(4)(b)): 1 March to 1 May 2016.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `rejected` (`d` 1 2 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2016) FALSE `any day` (`d` 2 5 2016) EQUALS TRUE
-- s 76(2): for a non-complying notice only a rejection keeps the right; a request does not, and there is no second step.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `bad form` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 1 2 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 6 2016) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `bad form` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 1 2 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 3 2016) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `bad form` (`d` 15 1 2016) `rejected` (`d` 1 2 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2016) FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 1 2017) EQUALS FALSE
-- s 34A(2): the Nominal Defendant, notified of efforts to identify the vehicle on 1 April, did not refuse by 1 June.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `no search` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 1 2 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2016) FALSE `any day` (`d` 2 6 2016) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the insurer lost the right to reject my claim` `no police report` (`d` 15 1 2016) `asked` (`d` 15 3 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 1 2017) EQUALS FALSE

-- Arguments: as above, then the Commission assessed in my favour; referred only for an exemption certificate.
#ASSERT `Can my claim still be referred for assessment` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `nothing done` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 16 3 2016) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim still be referred for assessment` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `nothing done` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 15 3 2016) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my claim still be referred for assessment` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `rejected` (`d` 1 2 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 1 2017) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim still be referred for assessment` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `rejected` (`d` 1 2 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 1 2017) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim still be referred for assessment` `late` (`d` 15 1 2016) `rejected` (`d` 1 2 2016) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 1 2017) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 81 -- liability`

`admits` MEANS `it admits liability`
`admits in part` MEANS `it admits liability in part`
`denies` MEANS `it denies liability`

-- Notice of claim on 10 January 2016: the three months end on 10 April 2016.
-- Arguments: day of notice of claim; insurer gave notice; day of that notice; what it said; today.
#ASSERT `Where does liability stand` (`d` 10 1 2016) TRUE (`d` 10 4 2016) `admits` (`d` 1 5 2016) EQUALS `the insurer admits liability`
#ASSERT `Where does liability stand` (`d` 10 1 2016) TRUE (`d` 10 4 2016) `denies` (`d` 1 5 2016) EQUALS `the insurer denies liability`
#ASSERT `Where does liability stand` (`d` 10 1 2016) TRUE (`d` 11 4 2016) `denies` (`d` 1 5 2016) EQUALS `the insurer is taken to have wholly denied liability`
-- s 81(4): a late admission still counts.
#ASSERT `Where does liability stand` (`d` 10 1 2016) TRUE (`d` 11 4 2016) `admits in part` (`d` 1 5 2016) EQUALS `the insurer admits liability in part`
#ASSERT `Where does liability stand` (`d` 10 1 2016) FALSE `any day` `denies` (`d` 10 4 2016) EQUALS `the insurer still has time to answer`
#ASSERT `Where does liability stand` (`d` 10 1 2016) FALSE `any day` `denies` (`d` 11 4 2016) EQUALS `the insurer is taken to have wholly denied liability`
#ASSERT `Where does liability stand` (`d` 10 1 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2016) `admits in part` (`d` 1 5 2016) EQUALS `the insurer admits liability in part`

§§ `s 82 -- the offer of settlement`

-- Accident on 1 January 2015. Arguments: accident; death; insurer wholly denies; assessor declined; recovered; when; particulars provided; when.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2016) EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 9 2016)
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 31 12 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2016) EQUALS JUST (`d` 31 1 2017)
-- 31 January plus a month is 29 February 2016; 1 December 2015 plus two months is 1 February 2016.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 31 1 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 12 2015) EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 2 2016)
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2016) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2016) FALSE `any day` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Recovered on the third anniversary: within 3 years. A day later: s 82(4)(b).
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2018) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2017) EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 2 2018)
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer make me an offer` (`d` 1 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 1 2018) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2017) EQUALS NOTHING

